<article class="env-lemma" id="03Y1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03Y1">Lemma <span data-tag="03Y1">80.3.8</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ F \ar[r]^ a &  G \ar[r]^ b &  H }  \]
</div>
  <p> be maps of presheaves on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. If $a$ and $b$ are representable by algebraic spaces, so is $b \circ a$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $T$ be a scheme over $S$, and let $T \to H$ be a morphism. By assumption $T \times _ H G$ is an algebraic space. Hence by Lemma <a href="/tag/03XY" data-tag="03XY">80.3.7</a> we see that $T \times _ H F = (T \times _ H G) \times _ G F$ is an algebraic space as well. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>